{"author":{"id":"f21006d1826991d76b358f177209294474e8c2701fc659ff8fe8b8f40ee77f55"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1775071995,"nonce":"XZiXL21sJQn0/WVJ5lGvveekyGc=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOCGKeh874s1Kh","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/1142#issuecomment-4172501665"},"message":"\u003e One thing i'm doing differently though is calling the git-bug.exe directly instead of using the \"git bug \u003c..\u003e\" approach, because i couldn't figure out how to get that working with just the exe from the Releases page :(\n\u003e\n\u003e Would that potentially cause issues ?\n\nno, calling the binary directly wouldn't cause any issues. as an fyi, the way you get the subcommand working is by moving the binary to somewhere in your `PATH`. when you invoke `git foo`, git first checks if `foo` is a valid internal subcommand, and if it isn't, it searches your `PATH` to see if a `git-foo` binary exists (in the case of windows, it checks for `git-foo.exe`).\n\n---\n\ni had some time and took another look today. the error you received:\n\n```\nError: Unable to start editor: exec: \"sh\": executable file not found in %PATH%\n```\n\nactually comes from `git-bug`: https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/blob/9b06f224354f3cf745ad6bf6620c1b04ca51077f/commands/input/input.go#L55-L69\n\nso what's happening is that whatever you have set `core.editor` (or `GIT_EDITOR`, `EDITOR`, etc...) to (presumably, this is `subl -w`) is erroring out, so `git-bug` tries to launch it under `sh`, which fails because that isn't really something we should be doing on windows, and then you're shown that error.\n\nwhat you need to do here is figure out what command you use to launch sublime text from your shell, and use _that_ as the value for `core.editor` (or `GIT_EDITOR`, `EDITOR`, etc...).","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1775072106,"nonce":"wf70Ku8PI6DxF4SXS2tBM0KvQ94=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOCGKeh874s3X1","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/1142#issuecomment-4172510709"},"message":"this may provide some insight for you: http://web.archive.org/web/20250711105026/https://stackoverflow.com/questions/8951275/how-can-i-make-sublime-text-the-default-editor-for-git","files":null}]}